Summary: CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX: upgrade OpenGL 3.2-4.1 context requests to forward-compatible
Category: graphics
Kind: feature
Origin: crossover
  Version: 26.0.0
  CW-Hacks: 24834
  URL: https://media.codeweavers.com/pub/crossover/source/crossover-sources-26.0.0.tar.gz
  Files: dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
  Changes: verbatim (CrossOver 26.3.0 has the same lines)
  Note: Sikarugir 10.0_8 ships it: winemac.so has the string
    CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX
Upstream: differently (Wine 11.19 and later accept such requests without
 it: 11.19 rewrote winemac's wglCreateContextAttribsARB without the check;
 11.18 still refuses them)
Why: macOS only offers forward-compatible 3.2+ core contexts, and the Mac
 driver of Wine 11.18 and earlier refuses a 3.2-4.1 context request without
 WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB, as Windows programs usually send
 it. With CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX=1 in the environment the request is upgraded
 to forward-compatible instead, as CrossOver does. The only difference for
 the program is that deprecated features (wide lines) are unavailable,
 which a core context mostly lacks anyway. Wine 11.19 and later behave this
 way without being asked, so their builds don't need the patch.
Programs: none known; programs that ask Wine 11.18 or earlier for an OpenGL 3.2-4.1
 context without the forward-compatible flag
Enable: env CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX=1 (each process that creates a context; only a value starting with 1)
Status: 11.18: 2026-11-28: carried from 10.0 (same hunk); macfixes 11.18
 build1 (CI run 46126808397) failed gl-core-context without it ("3.2 core
 context without the forward-compatible flag: refused")

diff --git a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
index 68de39f..b5e747f 100644
--- a/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
+++ b/dlls/winemac.drv/opengl.c
@@ -2824,6 +2824,14 @@ static struct wgl_context *macdrv_wglCreateContextAttribsARB(HDC hdc,
     if ((major == 3 && (minor == 2 || minor == 3)) ||
         (major == 4 && (minor == 0 || minor == 1)))
     {
+        /* CW Hack 24834 */
+        const char *fwd_compat_context = getenv("CX_FWD_COMPAT_GL_CTX");
+        if (fwd_compat_context && fwd_compat_context[0] == '1')
+        {
+            if (!(flags & WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB))
+                flags |= WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB;
+        }
+
         if (!(flags & WGL_CONTEXT_FORWARD_COMPATIBLE_BIT_ARB))
         {
             WARN("OS X only supports forward-compatible 3.2+ contexts\n");
